    "description": "If you want capacity without spending much, the Bloem Classic is the straightforward answer. Retailers list it at 256 fluid ounces, a true 2 gallons, with a removable nozzle so you can pour a direct stream into a large pot or put the rose back on for a shower over a bed. Because it is plastic, the empty can weighs very little, but remember that 2 gallons of water is close to 17 pounds, so this is a can for adults watering beds and borders rather than a can to carry up and down stairs. The plastic rose is functional rather than fine; it produces a heavier spray than a brass rose and is not the right tool for flats of tiny seedlings. Bloem sells it in a wide range of colours and it turns up at most hardware and garden stores, often at a lower price than anything else here. It is the sensible choice for a fertilizer can too, so you can keep a better metal can for plain water. Do not leave it full in hard frost."
